&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Directions: In each of the following questions, there are six sentences marked S1, S6, P, Q, R, S. The positions of S1 and S6 are fixed. You are required to choose one of the four alternatives which would be the most logical sequence of the sentences in the passage.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;S1. Holi is an important festival to Hindus, who believe it to be a&amp;nbsp; time for enjoying spring&amp;#39;s abundant colours and saying farewell to winter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;P. It is celebrated at the end of winter, on the last full moon day of the lunar month Phalgun (February/March), (Phalgun Purnima), which usually falls in March, sometimes in late February.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Q. In 17th century literature, it was identified as a festival that celebrated agriculture, commemorated good spring harvests and the fertile land.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;R. &amp;nbsp;To many Hindus, Holi festivities mark the beginning of the new year.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;S. The festival has many purposes; most prominently, it celebrates the beginning of Spring.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;S6. It is also an occasion to reset and renew ruptured relationships, end conflicts and rid themselves of accumulated emotional impurities from the past.&lt;/p&gt;
